    <item>
      <title>Hey, Listen! Navi in TotK</title>
      <author>zapiltar</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/744196</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/744196#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">fbddddef2038a571b8bc83d2e75d6d8f6a2844df</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:23:56 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b02f5ad0acec.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b02f5d417e77.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b02f66ebee21.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b0599c061380.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b0599c066167.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b0599c0f0984.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; TKMM Version Separation&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Separated TKMM 1.4.3 and TKMM 1.2.1 into two separate zip files to avoid confusion with them packed together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Hey, Listen!&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod brings Navi, the Hero of Time's trusty companion to Tears of the Kingdom!&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In v2.0, Navi acts as a lite sage. She has a new ability to guide Link to nearby secrets; Chests, Koroks, and undiscovered Shrines!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can now toggle the vocal performance right in the game via her Key Item, aswell as enable and disable her power as you wish! She can be summoned and dismissed; enabling and disabling the vanilla lock on arrows to allow her to act as the lock on arrow when summoned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Installation Guide&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Emulators&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Ryujinx/Ryubing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Right click TOTK &amp;gt; Open Mods Directory&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy Navi folder from the TotK &lt;version&gt;/Emulator to the opened folder&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Eden/Yuzu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Right click TOTK &amp;gt; Open Mod Data Location&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy Navi folder from the TotK &lt;version&gt;/Emulator to the opened folder&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Enable Navi in the &lt;i&gt;TOTK &amp;gt; Properties &amp;gt; Add-Ons &lt;/i&gt;menu&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;TotK valentderah Recomp&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy the Navi folder from TotK 1.4.3/Emulator into both:&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;recomp_path&gt;\Build\mods\&lt;/recomp_path&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;recomp_path&gt;\Runs\(ModpackName)&lt;your_run&gt;\mods\&lt;/your_run&gt;&lt;/recomp_path&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&amp;nbsp;- In the recomp's Mods tab, click Rebuild the game now&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Optional .pchtxt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;- In Navi/exefs replace the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;.ips&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;with the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;.pchtxt&lt;/span&gt; from Optional pchtxt/TotK &lt;version&gt;/&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This only works for the emulators and recompilations&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Hardware&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;FIRMWARE &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;23.5.0+ | AMS 1.12.2+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Copy atmosphere from TotK &lt;version&gt;/Switch to the root of the SD card it should create:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;SD:/atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/romfs/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;SD:/atmosphere/exefs_patches/Navi/&lt;build_id&gt;.ips&lt;/build_id&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;TKMM Install&lt;/h1&gt;- Point TKMM to your TotK dump&lt;br&gt;- Set the language to your game's.&lt;br&gt;- Import the edition that matches your game patch; either 1.4.3 or 1.2.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Drag the correct version into TKMM&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;- Keep Navi enabled, then Merge.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;TKMM Recomp Install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Unzip the _ModManager.zip, drag the matching game version tkcl into TKMM&lt;br&gt;- Set the merge output to your run's mod folder: &lt;recomp&gt;\Runs\&lt;runname&gt;(ModpackName)\mods&lt;br&gt;- Merge&lt;br&gt;- Copy Navi's code patch to the correct location:&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;In the merged output open exefs, and copy the&amp;nbsp;277178B7DBA1B6D4949A84778D4ABC58B31B34F5.ips or&amp;nbsp;9B4E43650501A4D4489B4BBFDB740F26AF3CF850.ips&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Paste it into &lt;recomp&gt;\Builds\mods\(TKMM Output Folder Name)&lt;tkmm merged="" mod="" folder="" name=""&gt;\exefs\&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - If the folder doesn't exist, make it and make sure the names are exactly the same&lt;/tkmm&gt;&lt;/recomp&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;- In the recomp mods list, hit Rebuild the game now and wait for it to finish&lt;br&gt;- You should get Navi after the Purah Pad or a few seconds after the game loads if you're past that point already.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;TKMM doesn't merge effect/sound link files yet, if another mod shows an elink or slink put Navi above the mod or she loses her glow, trail, chime and voice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Updating&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Be sure to delete all of the old files before updating the mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Mod Settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In game you can change her Vocal performance between OoTR: English, OoTR: Japanese, and the N64 original voice, and enable and disable her ability. Use the settings.txt to change her volume, chatter frequency and the ability cooldown in seconds.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Emu/Recomp:&lt;/b&gt; Navi/romfs/Navi/settings.txt&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hardware:&lt;/b&gt; SD:/atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/romfs/Navi/settings.txt&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;TKMM:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;merge output=""&gt;/romfs/Navi/settings.txt&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Tested&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod was made for and tested on TotK 1.2.1 and 1.4.3 on the Ryubing emulator and on hardware running FW 23.5.0 and AMS 1.12.2.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;AI Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Claude Code was used for the reverse engineering and as a programming assistant to understand the game memory and code addresses that are used to hook Navi to each of Link's and the game states, trigger sounds, and change npc states.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Planned Features&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h1&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Sometimes Navi's sparkly sound will cut off abruptly&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Other Releases&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/742763"&gt;BotW Cemu 1.5.0 Edition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/743088"&gt;BotW Switch 1.6.0/1.9.0 Edition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/merge&gt;&lt;/runname&gt;&lt;/recomp&gt;&lt;/version&gt;&lt;/version&gt;&lt;/version&gt;&lt;/version&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/navi_totk_v20.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/navi_totk_v20_tkmm_121.zip" type="application/zip"/>
