    <item>
      <title>Ordeal of the Demon King</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">588521553e1abaa0afb234f50394b0f9894c5daf</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:30:58 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8e02dee7d8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd4486bca.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd44959b4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd449830e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd44c12aa.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6b006e2bdb26c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; v4.1.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Now you can challenge Ganondorf to a duel anywhere&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Improvement&lt;/em&gt;: The Blood Moon call&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: Minor bugfixes&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/strong&gt;. Bow model and texture by &lt;strong&gt;The Hidden Yiga Clan&lt;/strong&gt;. Made using Claude Opus 5 and 5.5 by Anthropic.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Ordeal of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"You have faced monsters, Dragons, and gods. But have you ever stood before the Demon King himself?"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ganondorf stands, and he is waiting for you. Not for a battle. He has watched the bearer of the Master Sword from afar, counted his victories, and now he intends to find out for himself whether the hero is worth anything at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a full quest line: dialogue, choices that stick, a duel against the Demon King himself, three commissions that end with weapons no one else in Hyrule can give you - and, for those who survive him, paths no one else can open.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
He offers you a choice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Kneel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Or refuse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose carefully. The Demon King does not offer his mercy twice.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Those who bow before him earn something granted to almost no one: the chance to prove themselves in single combat - against him.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The moment you accept, darkness falls. When it lifts, the sky has turned the red of a Blood Moon, an unseen wall has closed around the ground he chose, and the Demon King stands before you in his true form, his life written across the top of your screen: &lt;strong&gt;Warlord of the Ordeal&lt;/strong&gt;. Nothing else living is allowed inside: this is a duel, not a hunt. Try to run, and the ground itself will bring you back.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Survive, and when the darkness lifts once more he will admit - grudgingly, in his own way - that you are more than another hero clinging to a dying world. Refuse the duel, and the ordeal ends where it began, beneath his gaze.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The King's Will&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A proven hero is a useful hero, and the Demon King has work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
His first commission sends you after the horns of three Silver Lynels, thirty of Naydra's spikes, and a horn taken from the Light Dragon herself. Bring them, and he will forge you a bow out of them, by hand, in front of you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Watch closely as their fragile light is consumed by my darkness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
And the world answers him. While he forges, gloom boils up around him and the sky and earth turn the red of a Blood Moon - and when the rite is done, the colour drains away again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The bow he hands over is not an ordinary one. Frost clings to it and never melts, it throws a faint light of its own, and it will outlast anything in your pack. &lt;strong&gt;And its arrows freeze.&lt;/strong&gt; Not once, not while a material is fused to them - always.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Read that twice before you install:&lt;/em&gt; there is exactly one arrow actor in the game, so &lt;strong&gt;every arrow you loose, from any bow, leaves winter behind it&lt;/strong&gt;. That is the price of the Demon King's gift, and it is paid by your whole quiver.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
But do not mistake his favour for friendship. You serve his purpose for exactly as long as you remain useful.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Horn of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Take this. A horn of my true form. A manifestation of the doom that awaits this fragile world."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Come back to him carrying his bow and he will ask more of you - if you are willing to hear it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This time he wants the horns of all three elemental Dragons, and two from the Light Dragon. What he makes of them is not a weapon but a piece of one: &lt;strong&gt;a shard of the form he has not yet taken&lt;/strong&gt;, fused from their elemental essence and his own dark magic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Fuse it to anything you like:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;+90 attack&lt;/strong&gt; - well past anything the base game offers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fire in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it sets what it strikes alight, explodes in flame, keeps you warm, and does not go out&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shatters armour&lt;/strong&gt;, fells trees, and throws further&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Shield's features: &lt;strong&gt;guard bonus, perfect-parry bonus, shield bash and counter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It cannot be sold. Some things are not for rupees.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Thunderstorm Spear&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"There was a spear, warrior. I wielded it before this world learned to fear me."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Bring him the horn and he will ask once more - and this time it is not a trophy he wants rebuilt, but a weapon he carried before Hyrule had a name for him. Thirty shards from Farosh's spikes, four saber horns from the silver lynels, and the horn of the Light Dragon again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Stand back. Let the heavens bear witness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
What he returns to you is the &lt;strong&gt;Thunderstorm Spear&lt;/strong&gt; - the same one you have seen in his hand at night:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;45 attack&lt;/strong&gt;, and a reach half again past any spear in the game&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It comes back.&lt;/strong&gt; Throw it and it returns to your hand - and it does not shatter on whatever it hits on the way&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lightning in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it electrifies what it strikes, bursts in a shock, and never runs dry&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guard bonus and perfect-parry bonus&lt;/strong&gt;, an expanded shockwave, a faster charge, and warmth in the cold&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaks a guard at 80&lt;/strong&gt; - more than two times what it was&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Iron, and no one told the sky. Carry it into a storm and see what comes looking for it&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No hand holds it.&lt;/strong&gt; It rides at Link's side, a little above and apart, point turned ahead - and it swings, throws and returns without ever being gripped&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The gloom is gone from it.&lt;/strong&gt; It answers to the storm now, not to the dark - and no one else can call it out of the gloom&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It is a spear, so it is fast; it is his, so it is far too strong for one. And it was never made to be carried: the Demon King's storm does not ask to be held.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Forged Anew&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Weapons break, and he knows it. Come back without the bow, without the horn, or without the spear, and he will say what he thinks of you - and then take the materials again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Did the storm prove too much for your grip? It answered to me long before it ever answered to you."&lt;/em&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King's Path&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Name a place, then the ground between here and it will cease to matter."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Once his trial is behind you and his first commission given, your conversations with him can end with a request: &lt;strong&gt;open a way for me&lt;/strong&gt;. He answers with the same dark rite he forges with - and then the world folds, and you are somewhere else.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Seven places, some of them closed to you any other way:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Old Throne Room&lt;/strong&gt; - the Sanctum in Hyrule Castle&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Floating Coliseum&lt;/strong&gt; - five Lynels, and the Depths all around&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Thunderhead Isles&lt;/strong&gt; - the storm that hides the relics of the Zonai&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt; - the very tomb of the prologue, where he was sealed&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath Hyrule Castle&lt;/strong&gt; - Gloom's Approach, the heart of his malice&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; - below the Depths themselves, where there is nothing at all&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Western Plateau&lt;/strong&gt; - ground beyond the walls Hyrule raised to keep its world small&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A few words of warning, because he will not give you any:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt;, do not walk on towards the Demon King's own cutscene. Leave the way you would leave anywhere else - by the map.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; means exactly that. You may arrive on gloom - do not let it take away your life. &lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Code of Honour&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"The ancient code is clear: a challenge must be answered. Name the ground."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Win once, and the old code binds even him. From then on you may always challenge him again - and the challenger names the ground: &lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;, where you first knelt, &lt;strong&gt;the Floating Coliseum&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;the Western Plateau&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;the Depths beneath Hyrule Castle&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
He keeps count of every time you come back, and every ground has his words for it. No sage answers your call while you fight him, and your fairies wait in his keeping until the duel is decided.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The code binds you as well. Leave a far duel before it is decided, and he will warn you - once.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Blood Moon&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Let Hyrule remember who rules the night..."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Once his trial is behind you, you may ask him for one more thing: &lt;strong&gt;call the Blood Moon&lt;/strong&gt;. The gloom rises, the storm comes - and the real Blood Moon follows: its moon, its scene, and the world reborn around you. At any hour.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This one needs a small &lt;strong&gt;ExeFS patch&lt;/strong&gt;, included for &lt;strong&gt;1.2.0&lt;/strong&gt; - the version this mod is built for - and for &lt;strong&gt;1.2.1&lt;/strong&gt;. TKMM installs it together with the mod; installing by hand, copy both files to &lt;em&gt;atmosphere/exefs_patches/OrdealBloodMoon/&lt;/em&gt; - the game loads only the one named for its own version. Without the patch he says so himself, and nothing else happens. A second package is provided without the request and without any ExeFS file at all.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King:&lt;/strong&gt; Ganondorf as he ought to be - imposing, calculating, merciless, and worthy of his title. His words are written in red.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choices that stick:&lt;/strong&gt; what you say to him is remembered across saves, and he remembers it too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The King's Trial:&lt;/strong&gt; a duel against the Demon King himself - under a Blood Moon sky, inside a circle you cannot leave, with his own life gauge and title, and a word from him when you have taken half of it.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Code of Honour:&lt;/strong&gt; challenge him again whenever you like, on four grounds of your choosing - no sages, no fairies, and words of his own for every place and every return.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Blood Moon on demand:&lt;/strong&gt; the real one, called by his rite at any hour (with the included ExeFS patch).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;His Wrath:&lt;/strong&gt; strike him, shoot him or bomb him outside the duel, and he answers with a line of his own - and your death.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nothing is a dead end:&lt;/strong&gt; every commission can be taken again if what he made is gone, and the hand-in is the same rite - not a copy of it.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three commissions:&lt;/strong&gt; hunt across Hyrule for materials no shop sells, and watch him forge them by hand - gloom, sound and a blood-red sky included. Lose what he made and he will forge it again.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three unique rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; a bow whose arrows always freeze, the Horn of the Demon King, and the Thunderstorm Spear - which no hand holds.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King's Road:&lt;/strong&gt; seven destinations across the surface, the sky, the Depths, and places the game never meant you to reach.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No new NPC clutter:&lt;/strong&gt; one existing character carries the whole thing. The only other change to the world around him: two wolves step aside, and nothing else alive enters the circle while you fight.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Specifications&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;For developers and modders:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host actor:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Npc_BaseCampSoldier_Hylia005&lt;/em&gt; - renamed, re-scripted, and given Ganondorf's pack. No new actor is registered.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quest logic:&lt;/strong&gt; EventFlow, in his own flowchart - branches, talk choices, pouch queries and autosaves. His first speech is chosen by the recent-talk flag alone, not by the hour.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Map logic:&lt;/strong&gt; three Logic modules (AINB) of the mod's own, cloned node by node from vanilla ones. One returns a player who leaves the duel through a vanilla warp event. One watches areas at his feet on the &lt;em&gt;PlayerAttack&lt;/em&gt; layer (and one for bombs) and opens his own conversation through his vanilla &lt;em&gt;EventSetting&lt;/em&gt; row. One reads the boss's &lt;em&gt;Dead&lt;/em&gt;, held for a second, and opens the same row for the victory.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The duel:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Enemy_Ganondorf_Miasma&lt;/em&gt; is placed on the host's own spot behind the duel flag, and the host is warped by his schedule to anchors just beneath it, so he stays loaded for the victory. The gauge title is a label of the mod's own in &lt;em&gt;Nickname.msbt&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The far grounds:&lt;/strong&gt; a session flag and &lt;em&gt;EventReserveBancChange&lt;/em&gt; to a start position of the mod's own; the same boss row is placed in each ground's tile behind that flag, and whatever would join the fight (the Coliseum's Lynels, the nearest Like Like) steps aside behind its negation. Five vanilla &lt;em&gt;SageUnsummonArea&lt;/em&gt;s (one per sage) stand over every ground. Fairies are taken one by one into a saved counter and handed back from it. The victory plays inside the boss's own death event, under a fade. Lines differ by ground and by the number of challenges, through two saved integers.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Blood Moon:&lt;/strong&gt; an IPS32 patch per game build hooks the emergency Blood Moon node of &lt;em&gt;Sequence/MainUpdate&lt;/em&gt; - the one the game uses when memory runs short - into a code cave that reads a GameData flag, lowers it, and raises the manager's "emergency" and "a moon is due" bits. The game does the rest. &lt;em&gt;DmF_SY_WorldReset&lt;/em&gt;'s emergency entry is told when the moon is his, and plays it as the midnight one: no reload, no second moon.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boss events:&lt;/strong&gt; the half-strength line and the death request go through two borrowed vanilla rows of &lt;em&gt;BossBattle_Common&lt;/em&gt; (two Depths transform entries), each behind a switch on the duel flag - with the flag down, the vanilla flow runs untouched. The line is a &lt;em&gt;VoicePlayActor&lt;/em&gt; subtitle; the boss is held in &lt;em&gt;Wait&lt;/em&gt; and handed back with &lt;em&gt;EventPlayASForTimelineToInGame&lt;/em&gt;; the event ends in an &lt;em&gt;EventTransition&lt;/em&gt;, as every vanilla boss event does, or the boss stays invincible.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The boss's pack:&lt;/strong&gt; two bytes changed in place, no rebuild - &lt;em&gt;IsMiddleDemoReaction&lt;/em&gt; starts true (otherwise his mid-fight reaction waits for a cutscene that never comes) and &lt;em&gt;IsImpulseDamageEnabled&lt;/em&gt; is false (otherwise he wounds himself on the duel ring). &lt;strong&gt;The same pack serves the final battle&lt;/strong&gt;: there he will not kneel while the sages' scene loads, and slammed objects will not hurt him.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The duel ring:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;AirWallForBossBattleField&lt;/em&gt; - the only wall that holds when placed by a mod - with its visible effect switched off, raised only for the first duel. &lt;strong&gt;The final battle's own barrier is unseen too.&lt;/strong&gt; Wildlife is kept out by a vanilla &lt;em&gt;ForbidAutoPlacementAreaOnlySphere&lt;/em&gt;, present only during the duel.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physics:&lt;/strong&gt; every simulated actor the mod places is registered in its section's &lt;em&gt;StaticCompound&lt;/em&gt; (an &lt;em&gt;ActorLink&lt;/em&gt; plus the hash and index maps), or it would walk on the spot.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;His animations:&lt;/strong&gt; a private animation graph - a copy of the Hylian male graph with the boss's own clips cloned in: his battle stance, and a night drill of seventeen strikes and parries laid out twelve times over (a graph sequence does not loop, and one node holds at most 255 children). His spear comes from a private &lt;em&gt;EquipmentUserParam&lt;/em&gt; that hides it whenever it is not in hand; the schedule holds it only at night.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Persistence:&lt;/strong&gt; thirteen booleans and three integers appended to &lt;em&gt;GameDataList&lt;/em&gt;, with &lt;em&gt;MetaData&lt;/em&gt; grown by eight bytes per saved field so they actually reach &lt;em&gt;progress.sav&lt;/em&gt;. They are appended, never inserted, so an existing save keeps every field where it was. Nine more live only within a session and are never saved (six in the package without the Blood Moon).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dialogue:&lt;/strong&gt; Mals, built from genuine vanilla 1.2.0 archives. His lines carry the inline red colour code; your choices stay white.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teleportation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;GameSystemActor.EventReserveBancChange&lt;/em&gt; by named start position. Two are vanilla (&lt;em&gt;OpeningStart&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;StartPos_HyruleCastleIncident&lt;/em&gt;); five are added to the &lt;em&gt;MainField&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MinusField&lt;/em&gt; start-position tables, and three more for the far duels. The menus are steps of at most four choices - the most a single talk event can show.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Crystallized Ice Bow (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Bow_166_For_Ganondorf&lt;/em&gt;), Horn of the Demon King (&lt;em&gt;Item_Enemy_39&lt;/em&gt;), Thunderstorm Spear (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Spear_166&lt;/em&gt;, the Gloom Spear, its &lt;em&gt;Miasma&lt;/em&gt; subtype removed). All three are vanilla actors with rows in every registry - no new actor is registered anywhere.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Freezing arrows:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;NormalArrow&lt;/em&gt; gets the three fields that distinguish a Gleeok's ice beam from its ordinary one - &lt;em&gt;ChemicalType Ice&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;DamageElements [Ice]&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;InitialIceMagic&lt;/em&gt; - each in a file of the mod's own name, with a private parameter table. Tulin's arrow, which inherits from it, is pinned to the vanilla table. &lt;strong&gt;It is the only arrow actor in the game, so this affects every bow.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; inside packs, no file that other packs share by path is edited. A mod manager that rebuilds packs from shared files (TKMM) would otherwise carry such an edit into every other pack with that path - which is exactly how an earlier version froze King Gleeok's beams alongside &lt;em&gt;Depths of the Kingdom&lt;/em&gt;. These whole files are replaced and may conflict with mods that edit them: &lt;em&gt;Event/EventFlow/BossBattle_Common&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;DmF_SY_WorldReset&lt;/em&gt; (Blood Moon package only), &lt;em&gt;Pack/Actor/Enemy_Ganondorf_Miasma&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;AirWallForBossBattleField&lt;/em&gt;, the map tiles &lt;em&gt;MainField A-3, A-5, D-6&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MinusField D-6, E-4&lt;/em&gt;, and both start-position tables. Built and tested on game version 1.2.0.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The returning spear:&lt;/strong&gt; a boomerang in TotK is four things, not one - the &lt;em&gt;Boomerang&lt;/em&gt; subtype, &lt;em&gt;IsBreakByThrownAttack: false&lt;/em&gt;, an &lt;em&gt;Atk_Thrown&lt;/em&gt; collider, and the &lt;em&gt;Boommerang_Catch&lt;/em&gt; attention client (Nintendo's own spelling). All four are copied from &lt;em&gt;Weapon_Lsword_174&lt;/em&gt;; miss the last and the weapon will not even equip.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The spear that is not held:&lt;/strong&gt; its mesh is moved inside the model itself - sideways, up, and turned point-forward - because TotK gives a weapon offsets for crouching, riding, sheathing and standing, but none at all for the plain state of being in a hand. The sheathed pose has its own knob, &lt;em&gt;SheathTransOffset&lt;/em&gt;, so back and hand are set apart. The hit shapes stay in Phive where they were, so the spear strikes from the hand it never occupies.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Durability:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;MaxLife&lt;/em&gt; lives in two places - the registry row and the pack's own &lt;em&gt;LifeParameters&lt;/em&gt; - and the pack wins. Both are written, or nothing changes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource table:&lt;/strong&gt; every entry the mod grows is recomputed and shipped.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;The Ordeal Awaits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Stand before the Demon King. Prove your worth. And remember - he is the one deciding whether you deserve to live.&lt;/em&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/ordeal_of_the_demon_king_52bc0.zip" type="application/zip"/>
