      <guid isPermaLink="false">f4ab7015ce26e7448e4897275db8d3dcdeca4e16</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:06:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab3763e02e85.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab3763e3c729.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab3763e427fb.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Support TotK v1.4.3&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adds support for Tears of the Kingdom version 1.4.3 (emulator only, for now)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Fleet Sync&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Notice&lt;/span&gt;: I now suggest people download this mod from &lt;a href="https://hansoloblaster.dev/#mods" target="_blank"&gt;my website&lt;/a&gt; instead of here. You'll find the latest updates there. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fleet Sync lets you control several identical vehicles from one Steering Stick. Pick one vehicle to drive and link up to four others to it. They will receive the same steering input and correct their position and rotation to stay in formation. The driving vehicle is called hte controller, the others are all receivers. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is more of a concept than a fully fleshed out mod. There's likely to be tons of issues with it. But I'm having fun with the current iteration. Please leave constructive comments so I can fix issues and add new features. Some things won't be possible though. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The original idea was to just pair two or more control sticks together - but due to all sorts of physics and non-determinism factors, that didn't pan out to the "synced fleet" I wanted. So the code also actively steers the receiver&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Currently, &lt;b&gt;all vehicles must be the same build&lt;/b&gt;. This may change in the future, but it was too unreliable in this iteration. So autobuilt copies are ideal. Start by placing them roughly side by side on level ground. Small placement differences will be straightened into a row. If you noticeably place a receiver ahead of or behind your vehicle, it will keep that arrangement instead.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Controls&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stand beside your vehicle's Steering Stick and &lt;strong&gt;tap L3 + R3 together&lt;/strong&gt;, then release. This sets the controller.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Repeat beside another vehicle's Steering Stick to add it as a receiver. Different sounds confirm the controller and receiver selections.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Mount the controller and drive normally.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold L3 + R3 for 1.5 seconds&lt;/strong&gt; to clear all links. I forget to do this all the time before a new fleet. Don't forget!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;An negative sound means the selection was refused. (Remember, clear your links after you're done with old ones!)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Known issues / limitations&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Hoverbikes and Wing+Fans are the main tested use case. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Vehicles work but quickly fall out of sync due to terrain and obstructions...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Haven't tested boats yet. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Haven't tested weapon/attack vehicles yet - excited to see what people do with this. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Bad starting positions, particularly in water, can still cause problems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Receivers pass through trees, loose objects and characters while active so they don't constantly get left behind. They still collide with the ground and some scenery. Dismounting restores normal collision.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Clear and re-pair after changing a vehicle's parts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;Requires Tears of the Kingdom &lt;strong&gt;1.2.1&lt;/strong&gt;. Confirmed working on Switch and in an emulator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Uses &lt;strong&gt;subsdk6&lt;/strong&gt;. Don't install another mod using that same slot.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Code and detailed README&lt;/h2&gt;MIT Licensed source code and a more detailed README are available &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/fleet-sync" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The compiled mod also includes exlaunch, which retains its GPL-2.0 license.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/h2&gt;This mod was largely coded with the help of AI. In particular, models Fable and Astra. For an outline of how I use AI to make mods, see &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you enjoy my work, feel free to &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;! I provide the mod and its source code completely free and open source. I stand by that; so only donate if you're feeling friendly or would like to boost my spirits!</description>
