      <title>Bivvy</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/718525</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/718525#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">28888dd1b75f14947f0cc97cf3cc23bcd45e8bf8</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:05:19 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb09b57a6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb09d7056.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb09a7bcb.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb09c3f05.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb095ebb2.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb0955de3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aaddb0a52eed.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Support TotK v1.4.3&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adds support for Tears of the Kingdom version 1.4.3 (emulator only, for now).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Bivouac (Bivvy)&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Notice&lt;/span&gt;: I now suggest people download this mod from &lt;a href="https://hansoloblaster.dev/#mods" target="_blank"&gt;my website&lt;/a&gt; instead of here. You'll find the latest updates there. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod lets you create platforms that can hang from walls, cliffs and even float above the water. &lt;br&gt;This mod is nowhere near finished but by putting it out there I can get some early feedback hopefully.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Instructions &lt;/h2&gt;For full instructions please see the &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/bivouac" target="_blank"&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To spawn a bivouac you must first be climbing on a surface or in sufficiently deep water. You must also be at least 160m away from other bivouacs (for cliff bivouacs). This can be discerned easily by checking the minimap for any nearby bivouac stamps (a moon icon). If you see none - you should be clear to spawn one at your location. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Tiers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Tier 1: Spawns with a Hearty Truffle eaten while climbing or in water. Small platform with a cooking pot. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Tier 2: Spawns with a Big Hearty Truffle eaten while climbing or in water. Medium platform. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Tier 3: Spawns with a Big Hearty Radish eaten while climbing or in water. Large platform suitable for vehicle landing/take-off. Contains a "Beedle+" NPC who has valuable items to purchase. &lt;b&gt;NOTE: Selling your items to this NPC does NOT work. Don't try - it will break.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Warping&lt;/h3&gt;Once a bivouac has been placed, you can warp to it at anytime by going to the global map menu with the minus (-) button and selecting the crescent moon stamp at its location. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Known Issues/Frustrations&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sometimes warping to a bivouac will land you on terrain underneath the bivouac instead of on the platform itself. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Currently, placement of water bivouacs is too strict. If water isn't deep enough and far enough away from a shore, placement won't work. Also, bivouac's in the same body of water will tend to trigger the "proximity rejection" even if it is over the 160 m range. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Licensing&lt;/h2&gt;Mod is licensed under the MIT license as is its &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/bivouac" target="_blank"&gt;source code&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/h2&gt;Opus and Sol were used during development. For an outline of how I use AI to make mods, see &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you enjoy my work, feel free to &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;! I provide the and mod and its software completely free and open source. I stand by that; so only donate if you're feeling friendly or would like to boost my spirits!</description>
